{
  "text": " Then he took out his phone and texted his girlfriend, telling her to return the keys to his apartment by eight that evening, and immediately blocked her. I was stunned! I asked if he was rushing into this, but my brother said he could live with her not liking Lego. What he wasn't going to tolerate was what she'd said to his sister. That evening his girlfriend did show up, but instead of just returning the keys, she spent an hour knocking on the door and shouting, demanding to talk. And my brother didn't even come out. He sat at home, building that same castle, deliberately turning up the music so she'd know he was home but wasn't going to open the door. Eventually, she dropped the keys in the mailbox and left. Later, my brother admitted he'd been acting childish on purpose, since she wanted so badly to make him grow up. And the funniest part was that the whole time she was outside demanding a serious conversation, he was calmly building Lego, the very set that caused their breakup.",
